  "text": "A Tenacious character has a one-track mind. Once he is fixed on something he keeps after it. If a Tenacious character’s body of argument in a Duel of Wits is reduced to zero or below, this trait puts it back up to one die. This allows the character to play out the next volley (or more if the die isn’t lost). Once that one die is reduced, however, the argument is over.\n\nType: Dt (die trait). Cost: 4 pts.\n\nSource: Burning Wheel Gold Revised, p. 350",
